  "title": "Domain-Aware and Few-Shot Learning for Hyperspectral Fish Freshness Prediction",
  "summary": "A domain-aware lightweight architecture SGNet achieves 97.8% classification accuracy with minimal parameters, while a few-shot ordinal learning framework improves freshness estimation for HSI data. Both approaches address challenges in real-world conditions.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "SGNet achieves 97.8% classification accuracy with 4.75M parameters and a 0.64 days MAE.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The method outperforms scalar regression and label-distribution baselines on a 16-day salmon dataset.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Both methods are designed to handle real-world scenarios where data is sparse or noisy.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
